# Keep bundled Gemini voice samples in repo
!public/audio/voices/*.wav
!public/audio/voices/*.mp3
!public/audio/voices/*.ogg
# osg-audio decode fixtures: compressed containers committed alongside the .flac/.ogg ones already
# exempted below, because they cannot be produced without an encoder. Same reasoning and same class
# of bug as crates/osg-decode/tests/fixtures/*.mp4 at the bottom of this file -- without this
# exemption the generic patterns above silently drop them and crates/osg-audio's decode tests fail
# only on a fresh checkout.
!crates/osg-audio/tests/fixtures/*.mp3
!crates/osg-audio/tests/fixtures/*.m4a
!crates/osg-audio/tests/fixtures/*.webm
# Subtitle-benchmark fixtures: real recorded speech from reviewed CC-BY corpora (see
# tests/subtitle-benchmark/SOURCES.md), named and hashed by tests/subtitle-benchmark/manifest.json.
# The same generic patterns above silently dropped these too.
!tests/subtitle-benchmark/fixtures/*.mp3
!tests/subtitle-benchmark/fixtures/*.wav
!tests/subtitle-benchmark/fixtures/*.mp4

live-api-web-console/

package.json.bak
.port_processes.json
=0.0.6
=0.24.0
=0.104.0
# Anchored: an unanchored `bin` also matches a real nested source directory such as a crate's
# src/bin/, the same class of bug .gitignore already carried for `subtitles/` and `debug/`.
e2e/tools/**/bin/
e2e/tools/**/obj/
/bin
electron-dist
manual-dist-v2/
manual-dist/
dist-new/
.builder-cache/

# E2E harness dependencies (the lockfile is committed; the tree is not)
e2e/node_modules/

# Decoder geometry fixtures are committed on purpose: each one carries a geometry a decoder gets
# wrong in a specific way -- macroblock padding, a container-declared rotation, a non-square pixel
# aspect -- and regenerating with a different ffmpeg would silently change what is being tested.
# They are inputs to a real decoder, not stand-ins for a video a customer plays; the end-to-end
# journeys download a real one.
!crates/osg-decode/tests/fixtures/*.mp4
